  "findings": [
    "The historical corpus bypass recovered 24 labelled valid contacts (568 to 592) and added five confirmed false counts (5 to 10). Those five comprise four held-ball events and one ground roll; they are not all hand contacts. The walkthrough catch is an additional sixth case outside that corpus total.",
    "All six saved handling records stay uncertain under V16. Five contain no wrist landmarks in any sample, and each covers only -50ms to +25ms. A sustained-hold rule requiring 150ms cannot confirm a hold from these 75ms records.",
    "The walkthrough catch has wrists in eight saved samples over 300ms. At contact, wrist separation is 1.626257 ball diameters, above the unchanged 1.6 bracketing limit, even though the V16 radial allowance includes both wrists. V16 alone does not resolve it.",
    "Several second-ball windows alternate between small distant-ball and larger foreground-ball observations. This is an evidence-association concern; a wrist threshold cannot establish which person and ball belong together.",
    "The current handling-evidence collector also intersects its time window with frameIndex-6 through frameIndex+3. At 120fps that yields approximately 75ms; timestamp-based evidence selection is needed for a sustained-hold evaluation on those high-frame-rate inputs.",
    "A one-hand test was not invented or applied. These saved records cannot support a wrist-based one-hand test in five of the six cases. Obtaining sufficient correctly associated evidence requires rereading source pixels or otherwise collecting new evidence.",
    "No count changes means no additional labelled valid contacts were lost in this isolated experiment, but also none of the six newly exposed false events were repaired. This does not justify a blanket body-gate bypass."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Numeric saved-evidence replay only; no new detector, Vision, camera or live performance run.",
    "The 69 traces include before/after versions of the same clips; they are not 69 independent videos.",
    "Enabling the grip flag alone does not simulate all V16/V17/V18 pipeline changes or current selected-player tracking.",
    "A proposed one-hand rule is a separate, unimplemented change requiring its own positive and negative validation.",
    "Historical bypass also left seven uncertain accepted corpus events and two unmatched events; the walkthrough added 13 uncertain events. Fixing only the six known negatives would not establish release safety."
  ],
  "recommendedNextStep": "Retain the body gate. First collect cadence-correct, time-spanning hand evidence tied to the intended player and ball for the known bad events. Then evaluate a targeted hold/catch change and narrowly defined body-gate relaxation across labelled legal contacts, negatives, uncertain events and fresh recordings.",
